        <item rdf:about="https://www.nature.com/articles/s41563-026-02763-8">
            <title>[7] Bridging microwaves and light</title>
            <link>https://www.nature.com/articles/s41563-026-02763-8</link>
            <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><b>Last authors:</b> Paulina Plochocka</p><p><span style='display:inline-block;padding:4px 9px;border-radius:999px;background:#fee2e2;color:#991b1b;font-weight:700;'>Score 7/10</span> <b>B_IMPORTANT_CONDMAT</b></p><p><b>Why:</b> Magnon-exciton coupling in van der Waals magnet CrSBr; relevant quantum materials physics.</p><p><b>Tags:</b> <span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'>#magnons</span> <span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'>#excitons</span> <span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'>#vanderWaals</span> <span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'>#quantummaterials</span> <span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'>#CrSBr</span> <span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'>#spectroscopy</span></p><p><img src='https://media.springernature.com/m685/springer-static/image/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41563-026-02763-8/MediaObjects/41563_2026_2763_Fig1_HTML.png' style='max-width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:10px;' /></p><hr/><p><b>Abstract:</b> Strong coupling between magnons and excitons in CrSBr enables microwave-to-optical transduction, offering a route towards efficient conversion between otherwise disparate frequency regimes.</p>]]></content:encoded>
            <dc:title>[7] Bridging microwaves and light</dc:title>
            <dc:creator>Paulina Plochocka</dc:creator>
            <dc:identifier>doi:10.1038/s41563-026-02763-8</dc:identifier>
            <dc:source>Nature Materials, Published online: 2026-10-19; | doi:10.1038/s41563-026-02763-8</dc:source>
            <dc:date>2026-10-19</dc:date>
            <prism:publicationName>Nature Materials</prism:publicationName>
            <prism:doi>10.1038/s41563-026-02763-8</prism:doi>
            <prism:url>https://www.nature.com/articles/s41563-026-02763-8</prism:url>
        <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Last authors:&lt;/b&gt; Paulina Plochocka&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style='display:inline-block;padding:4px 9px;border-radius:999px;background:#fee2e2;color:#991b1b;font-weight:700;'&gt;Score 7/10&lt;/span&gt; &lt;b&gt;B_IMPORTANT_CONDMAT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Why:&lt;/b&gt; Magnon-exciton coupling in van der Waals magnet CrSBr; relevant quantum materials physics.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Tags:&lt;/b&gt; &lt;span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'&gt;#magnons&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'&gt;#excitons&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'&gt;#vanderWaals&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'&gt;#quantummaterials&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'&gt;#CrSBr&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'&gt;#spectroscopy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src='https://media.springernature.com/m685/springer-static/image/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41563-026-02763-8/MediaObjects/41563_2026_2763_Fig1_HTML.png' style='max-width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:10px;' /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr/&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Abstract:&lt;/b&gt; Strong coupling between magnons and excitons in CrSBr enables microwave-to-optical transduction, offering a route towards efficient conversion between otherwise disparate frequency regimes.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item>
    
        <item rdf:about="https://www.nature.com/articles/s41563-026-02766-5">
            <title>[6] Taking the heat off tantalum</title>
            <link>https://www.nature.com/articles/s41563-026-02766-5</link>
            <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><b>Last authors:</b> Tae Gyu Ahn, Alp Sipahigil</p><p><span style='display:inline-block;padding:4px 9px;border-radius:999px;background:#fee2e2;color:#991b1b;font-weight:700;'>Score 6/10</span> <b>C_MAYBE</b></p><p><b>Why:</b> Materials growth for superconducting qubits; relevant to quantum hardware and materials science.</p><p><b>Tags:</b> <span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'>#materialsgrowth</span> <span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'>#superconductivity</span> <span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'>#qubits</span> <span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'>#quantumcomputing</span> <span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'>#tantalum</span></p><p><img src='https://media.springernature.com/m685/springer-static/image/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41563-026-02766-5/MediaObjects/41563_2026_2766_Fig1_HTML.png' style='max-width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:10px;' /></p><hr/><p><b>Abstract:</b> Krypton-assisted growth of low-loss α-phase tantalum on silicon stays within back-end-of-line semiconductor thermal budgets while delivering state-of-the-art qubit coherence.</p>]]></content:encoded>
            <dc:title>[6] Taking the heat off tantalum</dc:title>
            <dc:creator>Tae Gyu Ahn, Alp Sipahigil</dc:creator><dc:creator>Alp Sipahigil</dc:creator>
            <dc:identifier>doi:10.1038/s41563-026-02766-5</dc:identifier>
            <dc:source>Nature Materials, Published online: 2026-10-09; | doi:10.1038/s41563-026-02766-5</dc:source>
            <dc:date>2026-10-09</dc:date>
            <prism:publicationName>Nature Materials</prism:publicationName>
            <prism:doi>10.1038/s41563-026-02766-5</prism:doi>
            <prism:url>https://www.nature.com/articles/s41563-026-02766-5</prism:url>
        <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Last authors:&lt;/b&gt; Tae Gyu Ahn, Alp Sipahigil&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style='display:inline-block;padding:4px 9px;border-radius:999px;background:#fee2e2;color:#991b1b;font-weight:700;'&gt;Score 6/10&lt;/span&gt; &lt;b&gt;C_MAYBE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Why:&lt;/b&gt; Materials growth for superconducting qubits; relevant to quantum hardware and materials science.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Tags:&lt;/b&gt; &lt;span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'&gt;#materialsgrowth&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'&gt;#superconductivity&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'&gt;#qubits&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'&gt;#quantumcomputing&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'&gt;#tantalum&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src='https://media.springernature.com/m685/springer-static/image/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41563-026-02766-5/MediaObjects/41563_2026_2766_Fig1_HTML.png' style='max-width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:10px;' /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr/&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Abstract:&lt;/b&gt; Krypton-assisted growth of low-loss α-phase tantalum on silicon stays within back-end-of-line semiconductor thermal budgets while delivering state-of-the-art qubit coherence.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item>
    
        <item rdf:about="https://www.nature.com/articles/s41563-026-02751-y">
            <title>[8] Magnetic control of an exciton–polariton condensate in a van der Waals magnet</title>
            <link>https://www.nature.com/articles/s41563-026-02751-y</link>
            <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><b>Last authors:</b> Florian Dirnberger, Rupert Huber</p><p><b>Authors:</b> Heng Zhang, Niloufar Nilforoushan, Christian Weidgans, et al.</p><p><span style='display:inline-block;padding:4px 9px;border-radius:999px;background:#fee2e2;color:#991b1b;font-weight:700;'>Score 8/10</span> <b>B_IMPORTANT_CONDMAT</b></p><p><b>Why:</b> Exciton-polariton condensation in a van der Waals magnet; combines magnetism and quantum phenomena.</p><p><b>Tags:</b> <span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'>#excitons</span> <span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'>#polaritons</span> <span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'>#magnons</span> <span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'>#vanderWaals</span> <span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'>#quantummaterials</span> <span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'>#CrSBr</span> <span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'>#condensate</span></p><p><img src='https://media.springernature.com/m685/springer-static/image/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41563-026-02751-y/MediaObjects/41563_2026_2751_Fig1_HTML.png' style='max-width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:10px;' /></p><hr/><p><b>Abstract:</b> Magnetically tunable exciton–polariton condensation is demonstrated in CrSBr, a van der Waals magnet, using microwires embedded in an optical cavity under photoexcitation. The observation may enable ultrafast control of condensate emission through coupling to coherent magnons.</p>]]></content:encoded>
            <dc:title>[8] Magnetic control of an exciton–polariton condensate in a van der Waals magnet</dc:title>
            <dc:creator>Last authors: Florian Dirnberger, Rupert Huber; Authors: Heng Zhang, Niloufar Nilforoushan, Christian Weidgans, et al.</dc:creator><dc:creator>Niloufar Nilforoushan</dc:creator><dc:creator>Christian Weidgans</dc:creator><dc:creator>Tobias Inzenhofer</dc:creator><dc:creator>Marlene Liebich</dc:creator><dc:creator>Josef Riepl</dc:creator><dc:creator>Julian Hirschmann</dc:creator><dc:creator>Imke Gronwald</dc:creator><dc:creator>Kseniia Mosina</dc:creator><dc:creator>Zdeněk Sofer</dc:creator><dc:creator>Ritaj Tyagi</dc:creator><dc:creator>Jan Wilhelm</dc:creator><dc:creator>Fabian Mooshammer</dc:creator><dc:creator>Florian Dirnberger</dc:creator><dc:creator>Rupert Huber</dc:creator>
            <dc:identifier>doi:10.1038/s41563-026-02751-y</dc:identifier>
            <dc:source>Nature Materials, Published online: 2026-10-08; | doi:10.1038/s41563-026-02751-y</dc:source>
            <dc:date>2026-10-08</dc:date>
            <prism:publicationName>Nature Materials</prism:publicationName>
            <prism:doi>10.1038/s41563-026-02751-y</prism:doi>
            <prism:url>https://www.nature.com/articles/s41563-026-02751-y</prism:url>
        <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Last authors:&lt;/b&gt; Florian Dirnberger, Rupert Huber&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Authors:&lt;/b&gt; Heng Zhang, Niloufar Nilforoushan, Christian Weidgans, et al.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style='display:inline-block;padding:4px 9px;border-radius:999px;background:#fee2e2;color:#991b1b;font-weight:700;'&gt;Score 8/10&lt;/span&gt; &lt;b&gt;B_IMPORTANT_CONDMAT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Why:&lt;/b&gt; Exciton-polariton condensation in a van der Waals magnet; combines magnetism and quantum phenomena.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Tags:&lt;/b&gt; &lt;span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'&gt;#excitons&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'&gt;#polaritons&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'&gt;#magnons&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'&gt;#vanderWaals&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'&gt;#quantummaterials&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'&gt;#CrSBr&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'&gt;#condensate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src='https://media.springernature.com/m685/springer-static/image/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41563-026-02751-y/MediaObjects/41563_2026_2751_Fig1_HTML.png' style='max-width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:10px;' /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr/&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Abstract:&lt;/b&gt; Magnetically tunable exciton–polariton condensation is demonstrated in CrSBr, a van der Waals magnet, using microwires embedded in an optical cavity under photoexcitation. The observation may enable ultrafast control of condensate emission through coupling to coherent magnons.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item>
    
